        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: beta releases require manual reruns after plugin publication",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe 2026.7.2 beta release path took many hours because independent validation, platform, npm, and plugin-registry work was repeatedly serialized or rerun. A beta could remain blocked on plugin ecosystem convergence even after the core release was already safe to publish.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Freezes a product-complete Code SHA and reuses its validation evidence instead of revalidating moving metadata.\n- Runs independent release readiness and cross-OS work concurrently with explicit caps, caching, timing, and resumable evidence.\n- Classifies evidence impact so docs/workflow metadata does not invalidate product proof.\n- Makes beta verification report live, degraded, or failed states without treating small plugin-registry lag as a core beta blocker.\n- Publishes prerelease core first, then moves plugin npm to ClawHub convergence into a detached trusted continuation. Stable releases, explicit wait mode, and plugin-only releases remain blocking.\n- Keeps the detached path safe: immutable parent-bound handoff, authenticated child identity artifacts, attempt-bound retry deduplication, cancellation cleanup, ambiguous-dispatch reconciliation, terminal repair, and always-uploaded evidence.\n- Uses GitHub's supported `return_run_details` workflow-dispatch response to bind run IDs immediately; ambiguous responses still fail closed and reconcile by authenticated correlation. Contract: https://github.blog/changelog/2026-02-19-workflow-dispatch-api-now-returns-run-ids/\n\n## User Impact\n\nExpected beta critical path: roughly 15–30 minutes plus platform publish variability, instead of waiting for the entire plugin ecosystem. Plugin convergence continues asynchronously and remains visible/repairable. Stable release confidence is unchanged: required ecosystem work still blocks.\n\nNo release was created by this optimization work. `2026.7.2-beta.3` predates these final pipeline changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Frozen base: `9d2f5d4dbb639ecfcb95b6f5772895534f687691`\n- Current head: `a7c66c2992bf12c09c74856a453e8300711e6163`\n- Release-focused suite: 516/516 passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29678303536\n- Current-head continuation contract: 95/95 passed on Testbox `tbx_01kxwz6ck898q6ksgdx16gmhe2`\n- Current-head scoped changed gate: green in 1m29 on the same Testbox; formatting, declarations, test-root typecheck, and script lint all passed\n- Whole-branch changed gate: green in 7m40 on a warm exact checkout; SDK surface/baseline, boundaries, typecheck, lint, and import-cycle checks passed\n- Full `actionlint` stopped hanging after disabling its already-ignored ShellCheck integration; structural workflow lint now completes locally in under one second\n- Workflow-sanity fix: 93/93 focused tests passed on Testbox `tbx_01kxx11355sh49ahy92h45gx0v`; scoped changed gate passed in 1m32\n- Embedded Bash syntax checks, `oxfmt`, and `git diff --check`: passed\n- Mandatory autoreview: clean after iterating through cancellation, retry, artifact-authentication, and run-attempt race findings\n\nOperational timing evidence also confirmed the intended workflow: warm lease reuse avoids repeated 60–100 second hydration/sync costs, while focused workflow tests themselves take about 3.4 seconds.\n",
        "branch": "fix/forward-port-2026.7.2-release",
